text.section:
The license fees to engage in the business of shucking or packing oysters are the following or as such fees may be subsequently revised by the Commission pursuant to § 28.2-201:

For under 1,000 gallons, $7.50;


For 1,000 gallons up to 10,000, $20;


For 10,000 gallons up to 25,000, $45;


For 25,000 gallons up to 50,000, $75;


For 50,000 gallons up to 100,000, $125;


For 100,000 gallons up to 200,000, $175; and


For 200,000 gallons or more, $275.
				Any person violating this section is guilty of a Class 1 misdemeanor.
